    {
      "id": "1544716442979664004",
      "type": "Reply",
      "timestamp": "2026-09-02T14:31:39.45+00:00",
      "timestampEdited": null,
      "callEndedTimestamp": null,
      "isPinned": false,
      "content": "yeah probe cards are nuts. had a friend who helped manufacture them, crazy expensive too. Used to be cantilever probes assembled onto PCBs, but over time they've moved to MEMS pins and photochemically-etched bumps/tabs due to density requirements. think they are used to test wafers more often than finished/packaged chips though.",
